WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.200
- Thanks to Curiosity Stream
for keeping "Legal Eagle"

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.300
in the air, which now
comes with Nebula for free.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.270
Get 40% off of both with
documentary distancing discount.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.070
Link in the description.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.830
Finally, at the end of their rope,

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.750
the police shoot more gas
munitions through every window

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.890
in the house to flush Seacat out.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.349
Something has to be done, and fast.

00:00:19.349 --> 00:00:21.620
(intense music)

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.470
What would you do if you lost your home,

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:25.410
not because of fire, or flood,

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.940
or other horrifying natural disaster?

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.838
What would you do if your home was taken

00:00:29.838 --> 00:00:33.450
and destroyed by the
very people you trusted

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.860
to protect you?

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.370
The police in your own community.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.350
For most of us, our home is
our most valuable possession.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.470
Not only in terms of monetary value,

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.980
but also regarding our own
personal safety and security.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.230
And don't forget about
the sentimental bond many

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.010
of us feel with our homes.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.680
We spend most of our time at home,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.280
relaxing with loved ones,
playing with our kids,

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.720
and celebrating family occasions.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.270
So is it ever okay for the government

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.677
to just destroy our homes without notice

00:01:01.677 --> 00:01:03.665
in the name of public good?

00:01:03.665 --> 00:01:06.240
Imagine that while you're
out with your family

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.540
enjoying a nice day of shopping,

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.362
the local police blow up your house,

00:01:10.362 --> 00:01:11.195
(explosion)

00:01:11.195 --> 00:01:13.540
reducing your sanctuary to rubble,

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.223
all in order to catch a felon.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.320
Frightening, right?

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.160
But it can happen,

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.396
and it did happen

00:01:21.396 --> 00:01:25.400
to one family in Colorado in 2015.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.420
Once the initial shock
of the family wore off,

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.053
they wondered will the
government compensate us

00:01:31.053 --> 00:01:33.623
for the total destruction of our home?

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.650
Well, that's the question
that we must answer

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:40.121
in the case of "The House
the Police Blew Up."

00:01:40.121 --> 00:01:43.200
(glass breaking)

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.470
Submitted for you adjudication.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:47.790
Summer time, 2015.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:50.400
A beautiful cloudless
day in Greenwood Village,

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.760
just south of Denver, Colorado.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.340
The happy family of Leo Lech

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.040
lives an idyllic suburban life

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:59.510
in their comfortable 2,000
square foot, two-story home.

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:01.250
They're a busy, working group.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.080
Patriarch Leo and his wife,

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.370
their son John and his young family.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:07.440
The weeks are rushed, and seem to fly by,

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.130
but they get to relax just
a little on the weekends.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.660
As it is for many Americans,

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.140
their house is their prized possession.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.440
They take great pride in its appearance.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:18.830
And on this particular day,

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.720
the Lechs are planning a family outing

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.530
with the home in mind.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.566
As luck would have it,

00:02:23.566 --> 00:02:25.810
the family sets off on a fun day

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:28.020
of shopping for the home renovation.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.530
They're particularly excited
because they've been saving

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:33.700
for this home makeover project
for more than two years.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.810
First, they plan to visit a flooring store

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.990
to choose some new hardwood floors.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.320
Then they're headed to the home center

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.200
to pick up a few odds and ends.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.010
The only one not excited for
this big weekend shopping trip

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.910
is the family's nine year old son.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:47.462
He decides to stay back and take care

00:02:47.462 --> 00:02:49.773
of the Lech's two hunting dogs.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.530
Meanwhile, on the other side of town,

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:57.020
another man is planning a
very different kind of day.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.470
In a local Walmart, the
floor manager notices

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.110
a disheveled customer who
doesn't seem to quite fit in,

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:05.290
wandering in the electronics department.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:08.900
The customer, one Robert J. Seacat.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:10.652
Seacat thinks no one is looking,

00:03:10.652 --> 00:03:13.210
and he begins pocketing small electronics

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.890
and other items from the store.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:17.330
But what he doesn't realize
is that his every move

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.140
is being caught on the
store's surveillance cameras.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:22.110
The floor manager quickly calls the police

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.180
who arrive just a few minutes later.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.100
As the officers make their
way into the building,

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.050
Seacat realizes the jig is up.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:29.900
He hastily ducks behind a display case

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:31.740
and bolts for the exit.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:34.760
Luckily for Seacat, he
briefly evades the police

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.030
and escapes from the Walmart property.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:40.080
But without a plan, he
just starts running.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.180
Of course the Lechs are blissfully unaware

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.240
of Seacat, the botched robbery,

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.980
and the harrowing chase unfolding

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:47.550
on the other side of town.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.398
As they picture pieces of new furniture

00:03:49.398 --> 00:03:51.840
and other decorative items in their home,

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.560
the Lech family happily continues

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.410
discussing furniture options.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.240
As they finish shopping,
they're looking forward

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:58.461
to taking all of their new furnishings

00:03:58.461 --> 00:04:01.760
to their home in Greenwood Village.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.680
But Seacat manages to jump

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.320
into his beat up old pickup truck,

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.450
and speeds away from Walmart.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:09.220
But he doesn't get very far.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.720
The old pickup, which has
never been very reliable,

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:13.025
quickly stalls.

00:04:13.025 --> 00:04:13.860
(man screaming)

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.320
Seacat abandons the vehicle and tries

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.730
to evade police on foot,

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.580
frantically scurrying
around the neighborhood.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:21.760
While looking for cover, he
comes upon the Lech's house

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.630
where all is peaceful.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.700
Lech hurriedly approaches
the side of the house,

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.890
which luckily for him,
is obscured by trees.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:32.800
So he picks up a rock,
takes one deep breath,

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.625
and breaks the window.

00:04:34.625 --> 00:04:39.625
Little does he know, he has
just triggered a silent alarm.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.410
Back at the Walmart, one
of the witnesses tells

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.800
the police that Seacat is armed,

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.190
lending new gravity to the chase.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:49.270
More officers are immediately dispatched

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.600
to deal with the potentially
violent criminal.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.580
The Lech's, meanwhile, are
still completely unaware

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:55.440
of the break-in at home,

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.650
and that their house
alarm has been triggered.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:00.641
Don't forget, their nine year
old son is at home alone.

00:05:00.641 --> 00:05:03.000
But as far as they know,
they have no reason

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.470
to fear for his safety,

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.810
so the adult family members
stop for a quick meal

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:08.070
before they head home.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.015
But at approximately 2 p.m.,

00:05:10.015 --> 00:05:12.091
the Greenwood Village Police respond

00:05:12.091 --> 00:05:14.630
to the alarm triggered at the Lech home.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:17.370
Seacat has unlawfully
entered in his efforts

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.360
to flee police.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.110
Luckily, the Lech family's
boy hears the ruckus

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.630
in the garage.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:25.180
Terrified, the child goes
straight to the front door

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.360
and escapes from the would-be burglar.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.560
Fortunately, Seacat's so engrossed

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.230
in trying to steal one of the family cars

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.230
from the garage, that the
boy safely sneaks away.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:36.300
But the dogs the young son stayed home

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.210
to watch are still in the backyard.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.900
After further investigation,

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.160
the police learn that
this would-be shoplifter

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:46.890
actually has a record,
and a history of violence.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.600
As an officer cautiously
pulls up to the Lech's house,

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:51.640
and lazily exits his squad car,

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:54.020
bullets from inside blast
through the garage door.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:54.853
(gun shots)

00:05:54.853 --> 00:05:56.120
One of the bullets pings the police car,

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.880
missing the officer by inches.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.530
That changes everything.

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:02.040
If Seacat is willing to
open fire on the police,

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.070
what else is he capable of?

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:06.340
The police begin to
realize just how dangerous

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.250
this situation has become.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:10.330
At this point, the
Lechs still have no idea

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:11.790
of the potentially deadly situation

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.700
unraveling at their home,
but it won't be long

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.720
before they find out
their planned renovation

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.370
is going to be on a scale
they never imagined.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.240
The cops on the scene immediately report

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:21.340
the high-risk situation,

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:23.745
requesting back up, an
emergency response team,

00:06:23.745 --> 00:06:26.070
and a crisis negotiations team.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.570
Shortly after that call to dispatch,

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:30.190
Commander Dustin Varney
arrives on the scene

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:31.260
and takes command.

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.020
The situation escalates fast,

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:35.660
so Commander Varney finally
orders that Leo Lech

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:38.450
be contacted with a warning to stay away.

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:40.100
The news that his home is the scene

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.740
of a potentially explosive stand off

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:43.450
is a shock to Leo's life.

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:44.940
It turns out that Seacat is wanted

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:48.150
on several felony warrants
and is a known drug dealer.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:50.670
And now, he's in the Lech's family house,

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.660
armed, and as far as the police know,

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:54.310
maybe under the influence.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.935
Guns and drugs, a combination

00:06:55.935 --> 00:06:59.180
that makes the response team very nervous.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:00.810
Varney, being the man in charge,

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.530
starts making decisions.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:04.660
To secure the scene, he
has the home surrounded

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:07.060
and sets up tactical command posts.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:09.500
Then, Varney directs the
crisis negotiations team

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.670
to take over and try
to reason with Seacat.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:13.855
A tall order given Seacat's instability

00:07:13.855 --> 00:07:17.030
and the acts of violence
he's already committed.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:19.540
Still, the negotiators have to try,

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.010
tipping off a grueling
hours-long negotiation.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:24.320
And as the afternoon wanes,

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:26.256
and Seacats speaks with negotiators,

00:07:26.256 --> 00:07:29.480
he keeps hinting that he
might surrender voluntarily.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:30.927
He keeps telling the cops things like,

00:07:30.927 --> 00:07:32.921
"I'll come out, but I just want more time.

00:07:32.921 --> 00:07:34.630
"I don't wanna hurt anyone,"

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.980
and "I'm almost ready to come out."

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:39.300
But when Varney gives
Seacat one last chance

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.650
to come out of the Lech's
home peacefully, he refuses.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:44.250
So the police turn off his cell phone

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:47.140
and move on to the next,
much more drastic step,

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:49.130
a few minutes after 7 p.m.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.070
Cold gas munitions are deployed

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.210
through the first floor window

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.230
in an effort to smoke Seacat out.

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:55.720
But when Seacat remains inside,

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:58.210
Varney surmises he must be
holed up on the second floor,

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:01.460
which means he also has
the tactical advantage.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:02.970
If the police go in after him,

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:03.820
they could get shot.

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:06.147
Varney makes more quick decisions.

00:08:06.147 --> 00:08:09.740
Something has to be done, and fast.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:12.080
But all this time, the Lech's family dogs

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:13.620
have been in the backyard.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.040
At the sound of the first
holes blown into the wall,

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.590
one of the dogs escapes,

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:20.570
while the other pooch is still
potentially in harms way.

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.620
The Lechs notify police
that the dogs are there,

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:24.380
but the cops assure the Lech family

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:26.290
that their pets will be fine.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:28.730
Meanwhile, Varney has
to try something else

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.620
to neutralize Seacat.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.590
Still hoping the burglar
will tell the police

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:34.180
he'll surrender peacefully,

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:37.235
Varney decides to send a
robot with a throw phone

00:08:37.235 --> 00:08:39.110
to open up lines of communication

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:42.150
without allowing Seacat to
contact any third parties.

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.010
Of course, after all the gas grenades,

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:45.730
it's anybody's guess whether or not Seacat

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:47.540
will be willing to cooperate.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.160
Getting the throw phone into the house

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:51.090
in the first place is hard enough,

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.770
but the robot has to enter
the house to get there.

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:57.023
To do so, police decide to
literally blow the doors

00:08:57.023 --> 00:09:00.353
off the Lech house to make
way for the robot to get in.

00:09:00.353 --> 00:09:03.280
They use a BearCat armored
vehicle and explosives

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:05.350
to create an entry point
for the tactical team

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.860
and the robot, which they
send in with the phone.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:11.710
More than three hours later,
at approximately 10:40 p.m.,

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:14.090
the SWAT team enters the
residence on the first floor

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:15.573
and attempt to reach the second floor,

00:09:15.573 --> 00:09:18.200
one calculated move at a time.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.080
But Seacat has other plans,

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.624
and from the second
floor opens fire on them.

00:09:22.624 --> 00:09:25.035
The teams quickly pulls
back, exiting the home.

00:09:25.035 --> 00:09:27.770
Varney is losing patience
while the Lech family

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:29.040
is being kept at a distance,

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.470
unable to see the chaos
in their own house.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.100
Despite the continuous
ringing of the throw phone

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.528
and announcements over the loud speaker,

00:09:35.528 --> 00:09:39.360
officers outside can hear
Seacat reloading his weapon.

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:41.190
Four more hours crawl by,

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.530
and Seacat never comes out of hiding,

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.030
nor answers the phone.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:48.310
The exhausting night bleeds
in to the grim morning.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:51.220
At about 5 a.m., Varney
approves the launch

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:52.930
of another exploding device.

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:55.170
This time aimed at the
east side of the garage

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:57.290
in an effort to limit Seacat's movements.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:58.880
The homeowners still have no clue about

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.870
what's happening to their own house.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.319
Finally, at the end of their rope,

00:10:02.319 --> 00:10:05.570
the police shoot more gas
munitions through every window

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:07.400
in the house to flush Seacat out.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:10.610
They blow up virtually
every door and every window.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.890
All the while, they continue
attempting to negotiate,

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:14.490
but nothing works.

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:17.750
Finally, Varney takes out his final steps.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.800
Measures that will seal the tragic fate

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.550
of the Lech's family house.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.630
Varney orders the BearCat to open up holes

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:25.010
in the back of the residence.

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:26.437
Varney's exact instructions are

00:10:26.437 --> 00:10:28.514
"Take as much of the building as needed,

00:10:28.514 --> 00:10:31.670
"without making the roof fall in."

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:33.630
Varney's plan has three goals.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:36.310
One: to locate Seacat within the home.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:38.090
Two: to prevent him from being able

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:39.760
to ambush officers sent in after him.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:41.690
And three: to create gun ports

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:43.628
so snipers could, if necessary,

00:10:43.628 --> 00:10:46.350
shoot into the residence from a distance.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:49.100
And so, the police remotely
control the BearCat,

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:51.230
and begin bulldozing the house.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.480
Piece by piece, wall by wall,

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:55.310
they start to demolish the walls,

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:57.890
tear down the doors,
and open up sight-lines.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:00.350
The Lechs are about to get
that open-concept house

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:01.946
they'd always wanted.

00:11:01.946 --> 00:11:04.260
With the destruction complete,

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:05.780
Varney orders a tactical team

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.910
to arrest Seacat by all means necessary.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.370
The SWAT team rams through
the shell of the house,

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:13.870
runs up the stairs, and
bursts through a bedroom door

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:16.840
to find Seacat with a
loaded Glock 9mm handgun,

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.850
but they tackle him to the
ground and disarm him safely.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:22.303
Finally, the police take him into custody.

00:11:22.303 --> 00:11:25.620
Following his arrest, officers
located several baggies

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.500
of heroin and methamphetamine.

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:29.400
The police actions
throughout that fateful day

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:30.957
are designed to preserve life,

00:11:30.957 --> 00:11:33.090
and in that respect, they're successful.

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:35.050
No citizen, law enforcement officer,

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:37.820
or Seacat himself, is
seriously injured or killed

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:39.390
as a result of the incident.

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:41.350
Oh, and the pups are okay.

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:44.350
Shaken, dirty, but alive.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:45.457
As for the Lech house,

00:11:45.457 --> 00:11:48.820
well, that's a different story.

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:49.910
By the end of the incident,

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:52.250
the Lech house looks like it was bombed.

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:53.960
Giant holes riddled the outside

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:55.810
of the Lech house,
including the burst frames

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.220
of nearly every window and doorway.

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:00.430
The interior of the house
is a swamp of debris

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:02.610
from the battering rams and explosives.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.720
In fact, inspectors
declared that the Lech home

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:08.930
is uninhabitable, and a
danger to anyone who enters.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:11.550
However, after the shocking
incident concludes,

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:13.610
the police contact John
Lech to let him know

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.750
that he and his family
can return to their home

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.470
to pick up some of their belongings.

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:19.201
The officer also mentions that there was,

00:12:19.201 --> 00:12:23.480
and I quote, "some damage to the house."

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:26.950
The Lechs later describe
the scene as a war zone.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:29.290
When the Lechs arrive to the disaster area

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.920
that was once their lovely family home,

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:34.750
their reaction is beyond distressed.

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:36.050
Their hearts sink.

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:37.730
The scene is so bad that there

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.320
aren't any personal belongings to pick up.

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:42.680
They've all been destroyed.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.920
And despite the fact the
police told the the family they

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:46.420
could return to their property,

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:47.970
when they try to enter the home,

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:51.230
they are, unbelievably,
threatened with arrest.

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:54.040
The city of Greenwood Village
has condemned the residence

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.530
as completely uninhabitable,

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:57.680
and too dangerous for entry.

00:12:57.680 --> 00:12:58.680
So now what?

00:12:58.680 --> 00:12:59.880
Where can they go?

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.200
The Lechs aren't millionaires.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:02.890
They have one house,

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:04.180
their most prized possession,

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:06.720
which has barely been left standing.

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.878
So the Lechs appeal to
the police for help,

00:13:08.878 --> 00:13:10.370
as they have no where to go,

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:11.700
no clothes, no personal items,

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:13.760
and no home to sleep in that night.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:18.290
In response, the police offer
the family exactly $5,000.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.510
According to the police, five
grand should cover everything,

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:22.470
including their insurance deductible.

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:23.950
But while the police are confident

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:27.230
that the $5,000 will cover
a few weeks worth of needs

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:31.054
for the adults, the boy, and
two dogs, who have nothing,

00:13:31.054 --> 00:13:33.080
need food, shelter, transportation,

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.534
clothing and all the other normal items

00:13:34.534 --> 00:13:38.830
of daily activities, the
reality is much different.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.640
And although the city assists the Lechs

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:42.890
with temporary living
expenses in a gesture

00:13:42.890 --> 00:13:45.420
of good faith, no further crisis aid

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.970
or help finding new housing is offered.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:50.570
More over, the police
deny any wrong doing,

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:53.610
liability, or responsibility
for the Lech's damages.

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:55.720
The Lech home has to be demolished

00:13:55.720 --> 00:14:00.270
and rebuilt because it's
declared a total loss.

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:02.490
Sadly, the house in torn down,

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:03.597
and what's even worse for the Lechs,

00:14:03.597 --> 00:14:05.930
is that a precious heirloom ring,

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:07.952
one that survived WWII in Italy,

00:14:07.952 --> 00:14:10.670
is never recovered from the house.

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:13.120
And the young son has to
move to another school

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.900
because the temporary housing they have

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:16.610
is out of his district.

00:14:16.610 --> 00:14:19.260
Meanwhile, the poor dogs
are shaken to the core,

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:21.120
in addition to being covered in tear gas

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.470
and explosive residue.

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:25.310
So the traumatized pups are
forced to undergo medical exams,

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:27.600
deep cleaning, and a hair shaving.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:29.630
On the brighter side,
a dangerous criminal,

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:33.320
Robert Seacat is in jail and
no longer a threat to society.

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:35.240
He's convicted of nine counts of attempt

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:37.050
to commit manslaughter
with a deadly weapon

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:38.610
against a peace officer,

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:40.330
two counts of attempt
to commit manslaughter

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:42.426
with a deadly weapon, and
several other felonies.

00:14:42.426 --> 00:14:46.730
He's sentenced to decades in prison.

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:49.650
Even so, the Lech family
suffers emotional pain,

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:51.440
and a severe disruption to their lives

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:54.850
as a result of the sudden and
disastrous loss of their home.

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:57.050
The days and weeks that
follow are daunting

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:59.570
and stressful, especially
for parents trying

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:01.200
to provide a young child with physical

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.540
and emotional security.

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.880
Still, neither the police nor the village

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.550
offers further support of any kind

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:09.310
beyond the insufficient $5,000.

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:11.450
Enraged by the entire incident

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:13.910
and the damage that's
been done to their family,

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:15.860
along with the pathetic
handling of the matter

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:18.210
by police and the city
of Greenwood Village,

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:20.900
the family decides to
hire a lawyer and sue.

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:24.510
Mrs. Rachel Maxam and her team
of attorneys take the case.

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:26.530
The city and police
department are promptly served

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:28.020
with a summons and complaint,

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:30.970
leading them to immediately
engage counsel of their own.

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:32.960
The Police Chief, Commander Varney,

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:34.960
and all of the other
police officers involved

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:37.253
in the incident are named as defendants.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.850
Some of the proceedings begin.

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:44.800
It's a contentious fight with
the tensions running high.

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:47.040
The Lechs file a complaint
alleging the violation

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:49.640
of the U.S. Constitution's Taking Clause.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:51.200
The Takings Clause of the Fifth Amendment

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.814
requires the government
to pay just compensation

00:15:53.814 --> 00:15:55.929
to property owners any time their land

00:15:55.929 --> 00:16:00.040
or other property is,
quote, taken by the state.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:01.990
In other words, their lawsuit claims

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:04.640
that since the government
entity took their home away

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:07.210
from them, it was a
matter of eminent domain,

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:09.350
which requires the city
to pay compensation

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:11.180
for the entire property loss.

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:12.570
The city and the police, however,

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:13.940
argue that there's a distinction

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:15.450
between a regulatory taking,

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:18.000
where the government restricts
your property owner's ability

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.930
to use their land by
process of eminent domain,

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:22.750
and the state's use of police power

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:24.200
to protect the public.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:26.580
At trial, the Lechs lose
on summary judgment,

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:29.030
which means that even
if the court assumes all

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:30.630
of their facts to be true,

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:32.810
it doesn't amount to a
recognized legal claim.

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:35.186
Therefore, the case is dismissed summarily

00:16:35.186 --> 00:16:36.920
without a full trial.

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:38.590
In response, the Lechs fight back

00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:40.437
and take the case all the way
up to the appellate court,

00:16:40.437 --> 00:16:42.130
the 10th Circuit,

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:44.610
which hears the case
in the winter of 2018.

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:46.610
Will the appellate judges
see the case differently

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.130
than the trial judge?

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:49.670
Let's take a listen to the legal arguments

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:50.806
from both sides.

00:16:50.806 --> 00:16:53.820
(typewriter ticking)

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:55.430
- [Female Judge] Good
afternoon, counselors.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:58.010
So I have here that this
case is before the court

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:00.710
on the issue of whether the
defendant's complete destruction

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:04.180
of the plaintiff's home and
property is legally actionable.

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:06.100
Counselors, please state
your names for the record

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:07.990
and confirm that you're in
agreement that the issue

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:09.740
is just as I have stated.

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:10.830
- [Rachel] Thank you, Justice.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:12.643
Rachel Maxam, for the
plaintiff appellants,

00:17:12.643 --> 00:17:15.010
and yes, that is the correct issue.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:15.843
- [Andrew] Andrew Nathan,

00:17:15.843 --> 00:17:17.650
on behalf of the defendants appellees,

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:20.340
and we also agree with that
statement of the issue.

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:21.300
- [Female Judge] Wonderful.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:23.146
Then, Ms. Maxam, please proceed.

00:17:23.146 --> 00:17:24.540
- [Rachel] Thank you.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:27.760
Simply put, the Lechs are
seeking deserved compensation

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:29.790
for the loss of their entire home.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.640
The police destroyed their
house for no good reason.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:34.410
Yes, a felon must be captured,

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.320
but not by blowing up
innocent citizen's homes.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.100
It's patently unjust.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:41.950
Thus, the defendants must
provide fair compensation

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.140
to the Lech family.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.377
- [Andrew] May I give a brief response

00:17:45.377 --> 00:17:46.370
to counsel's opening submission?

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:48.400
- [Judge] All right, but keep it short.

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.680
- [Andrew] This case goes
beyond mere arguments

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:52.120
to appeal to emotions.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:55.070
We have laws to consider, to uphold.

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:57.000
In this case, the police and state

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.290
needed their rightful
immunity from prosecution

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:02.300
to be able to do the very
job of capturing a man

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:04.867
who posed a danger to society.

00:18:04.867 --> 00:18:06.070
- [Male Judge Number One]
Well, then let's get on

00:18:06.070 --> 00:18:08.700
to the applicable law,
the written briefs focus

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:11.610
on the Constitution's Fifth
Amendment's Takings Clause.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:14.060
So let's hear your oral arguments on that.

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:15.030
Ms. Maxam?

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:17.190
- [Rachel] Justices, we
submit that the trial court

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:20.100
erred in its interpretation
of the Takings Clause.

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:21.720
The doctrine of eminent domain

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:23.610
for which the takings clause stands,

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:26.379
applies to the Lech's case
because their home was,

00:18:26.379 --> 00:18:29.390
in effect, taken by a governmental entity

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:30.830
without their consent.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:32.640
Thus, the defendants must provide

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:34.779
just compensation to the Lechs.

00:18:34.779 --> 00:18:36.200
- [Male Judge Number One]
But the trial court found

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:38.230
that eminent domain only applies

00:18:38.230 --> 00:18:40.130
when the government takes legal title

00:18:40.130 --> 00:18:43.300
and ownership of a private
citizen's real property.

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:45.570
How was it mistaken on that finding?

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:48.190
- [Rachel] Because the court
arbitrarily drew a hard line

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:50.350
between the government's
power of eminent domain

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:52.020
and a state's police power.

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:54.750
But there was no statutory or case law

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:56.277
to support such a distinction.

00:18:56.277 --> 00:18:57.600
- [Male Judge Number One] So tell us

00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:59.110
what you think is the law

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:01.810
on the difference between
state's police power

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:03.600
and the power of eminent domain,

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:06.060
if you find any difference at all.

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:08.300
- [Rachel] I submit that
the law permits application

00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:09.980
of logic and common sense,

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:11.760
and that means the courts must look

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:14.221
at the ultimate predicament
into which the Lechs were put

00:19:14.221 --> 00:19:16.626
in order to decide whether
the preposterous acts

00:19:16.626 --> 00:19:20.950
and massive destruction done
by the defendants are a taking.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:22.370
- [Female Judge] So are
you saying that the purpose

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:24.930
of the taking is what makes
the Takings Clause apply,

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.610
and not the definition of taking itself?

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:28.443
- [Rachel] Exactly.

00:19:28.443 --> 00:19:30.610
Just as the U.S. Army could take over

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:32.130
an entire neighborhood of homes

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:35.450
because that spot is needed
for strategic missile placement

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:37.194
in order to defend national security,

00:19:37.194 --> 00:19:39.010
the Lech's home was taken over

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:41.010
as the place where the police needed

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:42.610
to catch a dangerous criminal

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:44.017
in the interest of local security.

00:19:44.017 --> 00:19:45.110
- [Male Judge Number One]
What do you have to say

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:47.880
about that argument, Mr. Nathan?

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:48.851
- [Andrew] May it please the court,

00:19:48.851 --> 00:19:52.010
I find it's wholly
unsupported by case law.

00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:54.140
Counsel conveniently leaves out the line

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:56.560
of cases relied upon by the trial court,

00:19:56.560 --> 00:20:00.030
which clearly separate eminent
domain from police power.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:02.105
Counsel fails to provide any authority

00:20:02.105 --> 00:20:05.230
that stipulates the circumstances
of the taking itself

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:06.830
are the controlling factor.

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:10.418
We must focus on the
legal meaning of taking.

00:20:10.418 --> 00:20:11.810
- [Male Judge Number
Two] If that's the case,

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:14.010
how should the court define taking?

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:16.010
- [Andrew] Simply the
way it's defined by law

00:20:16.010 --> 00:20:17.320
and in layman's English.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:20.920
When something is removed
from one person by another,

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:23.710
and when it's then retained
by the second person.

00:20:23.710 --> 00:20:26.420
Here, the state never
retained the property.

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:28.610
They only used the Lech home temporarily

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:29.870
for the public good.

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:32.040
The property has been owned by the Lechs

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:33.670
since the date of the event.

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:35.130
- [Rachel] That's nonsense, your honors.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:37.620
We must remember that
this was the Lech's home,

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:40.583
their residence, the place
which provided them shelter.

00:20:40.583 --> 00:20:44.190
And for a good 19 hours,
they were homeless.

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:47.210
Homeless is homeless, whether
the property was transferred

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:50.690
to the police as temporary
or permanent owners, or not.

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:52.280
The Lechs were literally prevented

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:54.150
from stepping foot back into the home

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:57.180
because it was declared
unsafe and uninhabitable.

00:20:57.180 --> 00:20:59.220
If that's not the police taking,

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:00.370
I don't know what is.

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:03.070
- [Female Judge] Mr. Nathan,
how is this case not one

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:05.002
in which the plaintiffs
lost use of their home,

00:21:05.002 --> 00:21:06.760
just like they would if its title

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:08.470
were transferred away from them?

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:09.910
- [Andrew] With all due respect, Justice,

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:11.200
it doesn't matter.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.050
Why?

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:13.670
Because this case involved action

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:15.550
by the state's police power.

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:17.810
It was not a federal matter
of national security,

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:19.560
or any other power that could lead

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:22.490
to a commandeering of a
private party's property.

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:24.460
The police power comes with its own rules

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:26.500
apart from the Takings Clause.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:29.050
- [Female Judge] Please explain
the main relevant difference

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:30.252
for the case at bar.

00:21:30.252 --> 00:21:33.010
Police power controls the use of property

00:21:33.010 --> 00:21:36.331
by the owner for the public
good, authorizing its regulation

00:21:36.331 --> 00:21:39.230
and destruction without compensation.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:41.730
On the other hand, eminent
domain takes property

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:44.360
for the public use, and
compensation is given

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:47.055
for the property taken,
damaged, or destroyed.

00:21:47.055 --> 00:21:49.680
- [Male Judge Number One] Ms.
Maxam, is Mr. Nathan correct

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:51.324
that takings under police power

00:21:51.324 --> 00:21:54.310
do not require compensation to the owner?

00:21:54.310 --> 00:21:55.380
- [Rachel] Yes, Justice.

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:58.140
But I submit that counsel
is misleading the court.

00:21:58.140 --> 00:22:00.190
What I mean to say is that this case

00:22:00.190 --> 00:22:02.510
is not about the difference
between eminent domain

00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:03.800
and the police power.

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:05.270
They are different.

00:22:05.270 --> 00:22:07.350
In this case, the police
destroyed the house

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:09.460
to protect the public
from a dangerous person,

00:22:09.460 --> 00:22:11.210
benefiting the public.

00:22:11.210 --> 00:22:13.290
The circumstances that
led to the destruction

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:16.050
of my client's home fall
under the Takings Clause,

00:22:16.050 --> 00:22:18.270
which means that they're
entitled to compensation

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:19.312
for its loss.

00:22:19.312 --> 00:22:20.650
- [Male Judge Number One] Please, clarify

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:23.650
whether you have any legal
support for that position,

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:25.695
because so far, we've only heard your

00:22:25.695 --> 00:22:28.746
and Mr. Nathan's personal
definitions of taking.

00:22:28.746 --> 00:22:32.410
- [Rachel] I'm citing a
federal court case from 2017,

00:22:32.410 --> 00:22:34.360
in which the court
clarifies a distinction,

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:35.670
which is controlling here.

00:22:35.670 --> 00:22:37.720
That court found that when property

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:40.850
is damaged as a result of
exercise of police power,

00:22:40.850 --> 00:22:42.870
it is not a taking for the public use

00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:44.025
because the property has,

00:22:44.025 --> 00:22:46.240
and this is the key part,

00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:49.200
the property has not been altered.

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:51.320
Thus, if the property is altered,

00:22:51.320 --> 00:22:53.460
it logically follows that the damage falls

00:22:53.460 --> 00:22:55.000
under the Takings Clause.

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:56.390
- [Female Judge] Thank you, Ms. Maxam.

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:58.790
Do you, Mr. Nathan, have
any cases you'd like to cite

00:22:58.790 --> 00:23:00.255
to dispute that argument?

00:23:00.255 --> 00:23:02.580
- [Andrew] Well, all of
the cases which I cited

00:23:02.580 --> 00:23:05.560
in my written brief to the
court undermine that argument.

00:23:05.560 --> 00:23:08.030
But to be specific
about the case Ms. Maxam

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:12.030
is referring to, that court
took the words not been altered

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:14.760
to mean its purpose had not been altered.

00:23:14.760 --> 00:23:17.020
To put it another way,
had not been altered

00:23:17.020 --> 00:23:18.770
meant not been changed in purpose

00:23:18.770 --> 00:23:21.610
to something other than a
private residential home.

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:23.390
For example, had not been altered

00:23:23.390 --> 00:23:25.110
to become a blood drive facility,

00:23:25.110 --> 00:23:27.020
or missile command station.

00:23:27.020 --> 00:23:29.140
- [Female Judge] Any rebuttal
or closing, Ms. Maxam?

00:23:29.140 --> 00:23:30.197
You're the appellant.

00:23:30.197 --> 00:23:31.680
- [Rachel] Thank you, Justice.

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:33.880
I'd request that the court
read the reference case

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:36.427
on its own and see for
itself what the 2017 court

00:23:36.427 --> 00:23:38.030
meant by the words.

00:23:38.030 --> 00:23:40.240
In general though, this
is a case where the police

00:23:40.240 --> 00:23:42.971
used my client's home to
conduct police business.

00:23:42.971 --> 00:23:45.547
Thus, it was taken out of
my client's possession,

00:23:45.547 --> 00:23:48.490
completely taken away by
its total destruction,

00:23:48.490 --> 00:23:49.890
its purpose altered,

00:23:49.890 --> 00:23:51.970
and thus having been used in such a way,

00:23:51.970 --> 00:23:54.570
it by definition falls
under the Takings Clause.

00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:57.660
And this court should reverse
the trial courts dismissal.

00:23:57.660 --> 00:23:58.980
Thank you for your time.

00:23:58.980 --> 00:24:00.960
- [Female Judge] All right,
thank you, Ms. Maxam.

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:02.200
Court is adjourned.

00:24:02.200 --> 00:24:05.350
